# Menu buttons (#1021): Set captures the virtual pad's next button for a menu intent, and writes no game binding.  North (Y)
# becomes Confirm; Y was Favorite's, so the two swap (Favorite takes Confirm's old button, South).
11800  expect capturing=0
11800  capture nav:confirm
11840  expect capturing=1
11840  pad tap y
11880  expect capturing=0
11880  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:by
11880  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:ba
# Default on one half of the swap puts both back: no two intents on one button, and no stray key.
11880  navdefault confirm
11920  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:absent
11920  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:absent
# A reserved button is refused and writes nothing: the D-pad moves, so it cannot be a menu button.
11920  capture nav:back
11960  pad tap dpup
12000  expect capturing=0
12000  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# So is the button that opens the controls overlay (the pad's C_HELP, the touchpad button), as the TV-menu button is.
12000  capture nav:back
12040  pad tap touchpad
12080  expect capturing=0
12080  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# Esc cancels a menu-button capture without writing anything.
12080  capture nav:search
12120  key tap Escape
12160  expect capturing=0
12160  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.search:absent

# A core option changed inside the in-game menu reaches the core once the menu is closed.  Down x5 from Resume is Settings (Save state,
# Load state, Achievements, Overlays, Settings), A opens the screen (the groups, on Video: `settings-group` puts the shell's memory
# there, so no count of rail items is needed), A opens Video (the core's category of that name: it is a TV Settings group like the app's),
# Down x2 is Internal resolution (Fast blitter, True color, then it), Right steps it from the core's default (1x) to 2x; B x3 is rows -> groups -> the menu -> Resume.  The write is a posted command: the value is read after the menu
# has closed and the paused core has had its boundary.
12200   load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
12240   expect loaded=1
12240   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:absent
12240   settings-group core:video
12240   key tap F4
12280   expect menu-open=1
12280   pad tap dpdown
12290   pad tap dpdown
12300   pad tap dpdown
12310   pad tap dpdown
12320   pad tap dpdown
12340   pad tap a
12360   pad tap a
12380   pad tap dpdown
12390   pad tap dpdown
12410   pad tap dpright
12430   pad tap b
12450   pad tap b
12470   pad tap b
12510   expect menu-open=0
12510   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x

# "More settings..." opened from the in-game menu keeps the menu underneath and hands the pad to the window only.  Down x5 is Settings,
# A the groups (on Interface: `settings-group`), A its rows, Down x20 clamps on Desktop settings..., A opens the window.  The window's pad presses never reach the menu: two Ups and a shoulder button go to
# it, B closes it, and the menu is where it was -- the focus is still on More settings... (A opens the window again), and it takes
# two more B to leave the Settings screen and one to Resume.  Esc closes the window the same way.
12530   settings-group interface
12530   key tap F4
